diff --git a/docs/deployment.md b/docs/deployment.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c2e3357
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Deploying Fizzy with Kamal
+
+This repository runs Fizzy on one Linux server using Docker and SQLite. Kamal's proxy terminates TLS and routes traffic to the Rails container. Solid Queue runs inside the same Puma process, and the `fizzy` Docker volume preserves SQLite and uploaded files across deploys.
+
+## Before setup
+
+- Create an A or AAAA DNS record for the hostname you want to use and point it at the server.
+- Open ports 22, 80, and 443 on the server and allow SSH from the machine running Kamal.
+- Create a GitHub personal access token for GHCR with package read/write access.
+- Have the SMTP server address and credentials ready.
+
+## Configure the fork
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml` and replace:
+
+- `203.0.113.10` with the server IP or hostname.
+- `fizzy.example.com` with the public hostname.
+- `smtp.example.com` with the SMTP server hostname.
+- `noreply@fizzy.example.com` with the address used for outgoing mail, if it uses a different domain.
+
+Set `GITHUB_REPOSITORY=your-github-username/fizzy` explicitly if the checkout does not have a GitHub `origin` remote.
+
+Set `KAMAL_ARCH=arm64` instead of the default `amd64` when deploying to an ARM64 Linux server.
+
+Copy the secret template and fill it in (the copied `.kamal/secrets` file is ignored by Git):
+
+```sh
+cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets
+```
+
+`SECRET_KEY_BASE` must remain stable across deploys. Generate it once with `bin/rails secret`. Fill `SMTP_USERNAME` and `SMTP_PASSWORD` only if the SMTP server requires authentication. Generate VAPID keys only if browser push notifications are needed.
+
+The mail settings are also available as environment variables:
+
+```sh
+APP_HOST=fizzy.example.com \
+SERVER_HOST=203.0.113.10 \
+SSH_USER=root \
+SMTP_ADDRESS=smtp.example.com \
+SMTP_PORT=587 \
+SMTP_DOMAIN=fizzy.example.com \
+MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS='Fizzy <noreply@fizzy.example.com>' \
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+`SMTP_ADDRESS` and `SMTP_HOST` are aliases for the outgoing mail server hostname. The optional SMTP settings `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION`, `SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO`, `SMTP_TLS`, and `SMTP_OPENSSL_VERIFY_MODE` can be set in the shell when the mail server requires non-default behavior. The default is STARTTLS with certificate verification enabled. When `SMTP_USERNAME` is present and `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION` is omitted, Rails uses plain SMTP authentication.
+
+## Deploy
+
+Run from the fork:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+Kamal bootstraps Docker, starts `kamal-proxy`, builds and pushes the app image, and starts Fizzy. The proxy obtains a Let's Encrypt certificate for the configured hostname.
+
+Subsequent deploys use:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+The SQLite databases and local Active Storage files live under `/rails/storage` in the `fizzy` named volume. Do not remove that volume unless you intend to discard all application data.
